 "answer_to_user": "THE METAL: Gold futures (GOLD.COMM) last $4,715.9 — up 8.0% on the week, +16.8% over the month and +39.2% over the past year, in a clear uptrend (above both the 50- and 200-day) with accumulation-style volume. The 'debasement trade' is the driver: record inflows into gold funds as the US debt crosses $40T and central banks lift gold to ~27% of reserves (above US Treasuries). THE MINERS (separate from the metal — these are equities): the biggest are Newmont (NEM.US, ~$142B), Agnico Eagle (AEM.US, ~$114B), Barrick (B.US, ~$80B) and streamer Wheaton Precious Metals (WPM.US, ~$74B), then Zijin Gold (2259.HK), Franco-Nevada (FNV.US), Kinross (KGC.US), Fresnillo (FRES.LSE), Shandong Gold (600547.CG) and Royal Gold (RGLD.US). So gold the commodity is ripping (+39% y/y) and the miner cohort — led by Newmont, Agnico and Barrick — is the equity expression of that move."
